<BaseLayout title="Experience | Bhagyashri Patil">
<header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Experience / Product &amp; solutions perspective</span><h1>Technical depth.<br/><span class="accent">Business-first thinking.</span></h1><p>My background spans enterprise solutions, analytics, machine learning, and stakeholder-facing engineering. I draw on those experiences to approach product strategy and architecture challenges with both business context and practical technical judgment.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/bhagyashripatil/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Full career history ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/contact/">Let's connect →</a></div></header>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">01 / Industry experience</span><div><h2>From customer needs to delivered systems.</h2><p>My career includes work at Honeywell and Saviant Consulting, alongside subsequent senior analytics and product-company experience. These experiences taught me to translate business needs into technical execution across teams, systems, and stakeholders.</p></div></div><div class="experience-grid"><article class="company"><span class="eyebrow">Earlier experience / Engineering</span><h3>Saviant Consulting</h3><p>The earlier portfolio describes work on machine-learning and NLP models, automated reporting, AWS cloud deployments, and leading a four-person development team. Responsibilities also included candidate technical evaluations and KPI-driven alerting.</p><div class="chips"><span>Machine learning</span><span>NLP</span><span>Cloud deployments</span><span>Delivery collaboration</span></div></article><article class="company"><span class="eyebrow">Earlier experience / Customer solutions</span><h3>Honeywell</h3><p>Worked directly with customers to gather business requirements, improve reporting and dashboard performance, and establish hierarchical access for stakeholders—an early foundation in understanding user needs and designing workable solutions.</p><div class="chips"><span>Requirements discovery</span><span>Stakeholders</span><span>System usability</span><span>Business outcomes</span></div></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">02 / My approach</span><div><h2>From ambiguity to action.</h2></div></div><div class="cards"><article class="card"><span class="eyebrow">Product lens</span><h3>Find the real problem.</h3><p>Understand stakeholders, user needs, success metrics, and the priorities behind an MVP.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="eyebrow">Solutions lens</span><h3>Connect the pieces.</h3><p>Translate business context into viable designs while evaluating integration, reliability, and scale.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="eyebrow">Delivery lens</span><h3>Make it usable.</h3><p>Build iteratively, communicate trade-offs, and create solutions that help people make decisions.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">03 / Technical roots</span><div><h2>A toolkit, not a boundary.</h2><p>SQL, data modeling, ETL, Tableau, Power BI, Qlik Sense, Python, and machine learning are part of my hands-on foundation. I'm building further expertise in cloud architecture and AI-enabled solutions, with professional implementations distinguished from experiments.</p><div class="chips"><span>Product discovery</span><span>Solutions engineering</span><span>Data architecture</span><span>Cloud &amp; AI exploration</span><span>Stakeholder alignment</span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="section-row"><span class="eyebrow">04 / Next chapter</span><div><h2>Cross-industry opportunities.</h2><p>I'm focusing on product and solutions engineering opportunities in Boston, Massachusetts, and remote. I'm interested in the intersection of customer needs, enterprise technology, and practical AI adoption.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="/projects/">Selected work ↗</a><a class="button secondary" href="/about/">More about me →</a></div></div></div></section>
